 35CL    24MG(16O,APG)                 2007DE14,1976VA24         ENSDF    202509
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$                                    
 35CL2 H CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$                                             
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35CL2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35CL dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 19-Aug-2025)          
 35CL c  Also includes data from {+25}Mg({+16}O,|apn|g) in 1976Ke02 and         
 35CL2c  {+27}Al({+16}O,2|a|g) in 1991Ja11                                      
 35CL c  2007De14: E=70 MeV {+16}O beam was produced from the XTU-Tandem        
 35CL2c  accelerator at Legnaro National Laboratory. Target was a 400 |mg/cm{+2}
 35CL3c  self-supporting target of {+24}Mg. |g rays were detected with the GASP 
 35CL4c  spectrometer of 40 Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors and a multiplicity
 35CL5c  filter of 80 BGO scintillators and charged particles were detected with
 35CL6c  the 4|p array ISIS. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(ADO),       
 35CL7c  particle-|g-coin. Deduced levels, J, |p, band structures, |g-ray       
 35CL8c  multipolarities.                                                       
 35CL c  1976Va24: E=38 and 45 MeV {+16}O beams were produced at Fysisch         
 35CL2c  laboratorium in the Netherlands. Targets were 300 |mg/cm{+2} {+24}Mg   
 35CL3c  enriched to 99.94% evaporated onto 30 |mm Au backings. |g rays were    
 35CL4c  detected with a Ge(Li)-NaI(Tl) Compton-suppression spectrometer and a  
 35CL5c  three-Ge(Li) Compton polarimeter. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g(|q),
 35CL6c  |g(lin pol). Deduced levels, J, |p, |g-ray multipolarities and mixing  
 35CL7c  ratios.                                                                
 35CL c  1974Va13: E=36 MeV {+16}O beam was produced at Fysisch laboratorium in 
 35CL2c  the Netherlands. Targets were 100 and 300 |mg/cm{+2} Mg on 1 |mm Ni    
 35CL3c  backings. |g rays were detected with Ge(Li) detectors. Measured E|g,   
 35CL4c  I|g, |g|g-coin, recoil distances. Deduced half life for the level of   
 35CL5c  3.16 MeV                                                               
 35CL c  1982Ra25: E=40-51 MeV {+16}O beams were produced at the Argonne        
 35CL2c  National Laboratory. Target was 50 |mg/cm{+2} layer of {+24}Mg (>99.9%)
 35CL3c  evaporated onto a 50 |mg Au backing. |g rays were detected with a      
 35CL4c  Ge(Li) detector. Measured |g-ray yields.                               
 35CL c  Other reactions:                                                       
 35CL c  1991Ja11: {+27}Al({+16}O,2|a|g) E=60 MeV {+16}O beam was produced from 
 35CL2c  the 14 UD-Pelletron at TIFR. Target was 350 |mg/cm{+2} Al evaporated   
 35CL3c  onto a 1.8 mg/cm{+2} thick Ta backing. |g rays were detected with      
 35CL4c  Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, recoil distances. Deduced T{-1/2} for   
 35CL5c  the levels of 3162 and 8844 keV.                                       
 35CL c  1976Ke02: {+25}Mg({+16}O,|apn|g) E=43 and 50 MeV {+16}O beams were     
 35CL2c  produced at the Institut fur Kernphysik in Germany. Target was a 150   
 35CL3c  |mg/cm{+2} enriched {+25}Mg (99.2%) evaporated onto a Au backing. |g   
 35CL4c  rays were detected with two true coaxial Ge(Li) detectors of 45 cm{+3}.
 35CL5c  Measured E|g, I|g, Doppler-shift recoil distances. Deduced T{-1/2} for 
 35CL6c  the level of 3162 keV.                                                 
 35CL c  1989De02: {+27}Al({+16}O,X) E=140 MeV {+16}O from the the Stony Brook  
 35CL2c  LINAC facility. Measured particle particle correlations.               
 35CL c  1986Br26: {+27}Al({+16}O,X) E=65 MeV {+16}O from the Pelletron         
 35CL2c  Laboratory at the Universidade de Sao Paulo, Brazil. Measured |s       
 35CL c  1979Ta03: {+27}Al({+16}O,X) E=50, 60, and 70 MeV {+16}O from the NBI   
 35CL2c  super FN tandem. Measured particle-particle angular correlations.      
 35CL c  2001Pi10: {+12}C({+32}S,X) E=19.5 MeV/nucleon {+32}S beam fom the      
 35CL2c  superconducting cyclotron of the Laboratori Nazionali del Sud in       
 35CL3c  Catania. Measured |s                                                   
 35CL cG $R{-ADO} values under comments are from |g|g(|q)(ADO) in 2007De14.     
 35CL2cG Expected values are |?1.3 for |DJ=2, quadrupole (and |DJ=0, dipole in  
 35CL3cG few cases) and |?0.8 for |DJ=1, dipole transitions (2007De14)          
 35CL cG E,RI$From 2007De14. Note that a few I|g values in 2007De14 have very   
 35CL2cG small uncertainties (<1%) which is unrealistic for an in-beam          
 35CL3cG measurement with Ge detectors. It is very likely the reported          
 35CL4cG uncertainties are statistical only and the evaluators have added in    
 35CL5cG quadrature a typical 2% systematic uncertainty from efficiency         
 35CL6cG calibration.                                                           
 35CL cG M$D with |DJ=1 or Q with |DJ=2 are deduced by the evaluators based on  
 35CL2cG measured |g|g(|q)(ADO) in 2007De14 and others are from |g(|q) and      
 35CL3cG |g(lin pol) in 1976Va24. Assignments are not explicitly listed in      
 35CL4cG 2007De14.                                                              
